# Videopac Vault

A private, local browser front end for playing your own Philips
Videopac / Odyssey2 / G7400+ game dumps, built on the open-source
`webretro` project (RetroArch's O2EM core compiled to WebAssembly).

Nothing here is bundled or pre-loaded: no BIOS, no game ROMs, no
downloads from third-party ROM sites. Everything runs from files you
supply yourself, from your own hardware.

## Setup

1. **BIOS** - dump your G7400 / G7000 BIOS yourself and drop the files
   into `emulator/bios/` (see `emulator/bios/README.txt` for exact
   filenames).
2. **ROMs** - copy your PicoPAC's `.bin` files into `emulator/roms/`,
   keeping their original filenames.
3. **Run a local server** (required - browsers block local file
   access for security):

   ```
   cd videopac-vault/app
   python3 -m http.server 8000
   ```

   Then open `http://localhost:8000/` in your browser.

## What's included

- `index.html` / `app.js` / `style.css` - the library UI (grid, search,
  filters), reading from `games.json`.
- `games.json` - a catalogue of your 203 PicoPAC titles, parsed from
  PICOPAC-GAME-LIST.txt, with platform (G7000 / G7400+) and category
  tags.
- `emulator/` - a self-hosted, trimmed copy of BinBashBanana/webretro
  (MIT licensed) with only the O2EM core included. Patched so it never
  phones home for BIOS files (the stock version pulls BIOS from a
  public GitHub repo automatically - that path is disabled here; BIOS
  is local-only, from `emulator/bios/`).

## Notes

- This is built for personal, private use with hardware and dumps you
  own. It isn't set up for public hosting - see the BIOS note above
  and keep it local.
- First launch of a title with a missing BIOS file will fail silently
  in the UI; open the emulator's console (Menu > Console) to see
  what's missing.
